IN THE NATIONAL COMPANY LAW APPELLATE TRIBUNAL
CASE NO: Civil Appeal No. 714 of 2021
CITATION: 2023 SCC OnLine NCLAT 143
YEAR: 2023

CORAM / BENCH:
Hon'ble Judges: Ashok Bhushan, Alok Srivastava

PARTIES:
Google LLC vs Competition Commission of India

STATUTES & ACTS REFERRED:
Competition Act, 2002, Information Technology Act, 2000

KEY PROVISIONS & SECTIONS:
Section 4 Competition Act

LEGAL KEYWORDS & TOPICS:
abuse of dominance, digital markets, android ecosystem, anti-competitive agreements

================================================================================
                    JUDGMENT SUMMARY & RATIO DECIDENDI
================================================================================

Upheld major competition findings regarding dominant position abuse in the mobile operating system market, underscoring anti-trust regulations in digital platform ecosystems.

1. ISSUES CONSIDERED:
   The court addressed questions of legal interpretation under Section 4 Competition Act.

2. ANALYSIS & PRECEDENT CONTEXT:
   Having examined the statutory scheme, fundamental principles of jurisprudence,
   and constitutional safeguards, the Court reiterated the necessity of strict
   compliance with statutory procedure and evidentiary standards.

3. HELD & BINDING RATIO:
   The principle formulated in this judgment constitutes binding judicial precedent
   within its territorial and appellate jurisdiction.

